    "description": "## Summary\n\nExternal_Deal_ID\\__c is the key the CMS configures against, and two same-shape deals differing only by source currently collide into an opaque -002 counter instead of carrying the source that distinguishes them. \\*Solution: the External Deal ID flow includes -{Source_Code_\\_c} inside the base key, before the uniqueness counter — e.g. BETMGM-DIRECT-ON-CAS-S; duplicate → BETMGM-DIRECT-ON-CAS-S-002.\\* Extends BUILD-228.\n\n## Current state\n\nFlow `Deal_Before_Save_Set_External_Deal_ID` builds fxBaseKey = {TEST-}{Operator External ID minus \"OP-\"}~~{Partner_Code__c}~~{geo}-{vertical abbr}, queries Get_Highest_Match for existing IDs starting with the base key, and appends -002/-003… via fxNextSuffix (overflow guard at 999). Entry filter: runs only when External_Deal_ID__c is null → existing IDs are never rewritten (this enforces the no-retroactive-change decision).\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n1. Append -{Source_Code__c} (when non-blank, from BUILD-246) to fxBaseKey. **Must be part of fxBaseKey, before the uniqueness counter** — if appended after the counter, fxNextSuffix's RIGHT/LEN parsing breaks.\n2. Verify counter behavior with a duplicate-insert test in sandbox: fxNextSuffix derives the counter by stripping LEN(fxBaseKey), so including Source in the base key is safe by construction — confirm it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Existing before-save trigger; no new trigger.\n2. Two deals identical except Source (S vs V) get distinct base keys with no counter; true duplicates (same Source) still get -002.\n3. Source blank → ID format unchanged from today.\n4. Existing Deals keep their current External Deal ID — the null-only entry filter must remain in place.\n5. External Deal ID remains unique across the org.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n* SLC-side matching changes (CMS already sends Deal_External_Id__c verbatim).\n* Deal Number (DL-####) — Source does not join it (Kobi decision 2026-08-31).\n\n",
